// std.rt_float: nothing. The module is empty and the file is a placeholder.
//
// The two float printers, the shortest-digit search and the layout of the
// float text stand in std.rt now, which is where stdlib.md 2.12 describes
// them. The compiler names one runtime module and loads one.
// D18.1, D18.2, D18.3
//
// Why the file is still here, which is the one thing a reader needs. The
// compiler that builds HEAD is the last pin of tools/bootstrap.ref, and that
// pin's loader takes <std-dir>/rt_float.ft into any closure that holds a
// float (notes/compiler.md 8, invariant 3). std/rt.ft holds floats now and
// stands in every closure, so the pinned compiler asks for this name on every
// build. Deleting the file gives
// `std/rt_float.ft:1:1: error: cannot read`, measured on 2026-09-14.
// D9.10
//
// So the file goes on the day a pin moves past this commit, and not before.
// It declares nothing, and no module of the library or of the compiler
// imports it.
